{
  "dom_id": "step-q65877",
  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{x}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}$ for $0\\le x<4\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$",
  "worked_solution": "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi , & \\, & \\, & \\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our two equations for $x$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}+2\\cdot 2n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & x & =2\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{6}+2\\cdot 2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+4n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}+4n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{12n\\pi }{3} & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}+\\frac{12n\\pi }{3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(12n+1)\\pi }{3} & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{(12n+5)\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<4\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<4\\pi .$ So, the solutions are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{3}=\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{9}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
